Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> I am now able to enhance my divination spell skill from Skilled
> to Expert. But would that be of any advantage (say, would it be
> more effective, cost less PW to cast, etc.) if all my currently
> know spells of that type are already at 0% failure?
>
> Janis

PW-per-casting is always 5*SpellLvl if successful, and half that if not
(exceptions exist, but are (very) rare).  I'm pretty sure that spell
skills only affect failure rates; that would make advancing the skill
singularly pointless, assuming that you already know Magic Mapping
(which is near-essential, and pretty close to a must with characters
that can get to Expert or even Skilled at divination), since you won't
be getting any other benefits by advancing it.  Obviously, if "all your
currently know spells of that type" are like light and detect unseen,
you should keep in mind that there're higher-level spells around and
think about saving the slot anyway, if your character will need it to
cast them well.



